  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "According to the Manual’s account of section 15(1) of the Geneva Conventions Act 1957, anyone proposing to use the specified Red Cross or Red Crescent emblems or designations, for any purpose, needs written consent from the Minister for Defence or a person authorised in writing by the Minister to give consent.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part30/3/3/5~1",
          "quote": "Section 15(1) of the Geneva Conventions Act 1957 (Cth) specifically prohibits the use for any purpose whatsoever, of the following signs, without the consent in writing of the Minister for Defence or a person authorised in writing by the Minister to give consent:"
        },
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part30/3/3/5~1",
          "quote": "(a) the emblem of a red cross with vertical and horizontal arms of the same length on, and completely surrounded by, a white ground, or the designation \"Red Cross\" or \"Geneva Cross\"; (b) the emblem of a red crescent moon on, and completely surrounded by, a white ground, or the designation \"Red Crescent\"."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "manual"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Manual’s account also covers designs or wording sufficiently resembling the protected emblems or designations to be mistaken for, or understood as referring to, them.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part30/3/3/5~1",
          "quote": "(e) a design or wording so nearly resembling any of the emblems or designations specified in paragraph (a), (b), (c), (ca) or (d) as to be capable of being mistaken for, or as the case may be, understood as referring to, one of those emblems;"
        }
      ],
      "authority": "manual"
    },
    {
      "text": "For examination purposes, the Manual says an applicant may be able to overcome a section 42(b) objection by obtaining written consent or agreeing to an appropriate condition-of-registration endorsement that removes the need for consent.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part30/3/3/5~5",
          "quote": "To overcome a section 42(b) ground for rejection based on a purported contravention of section 15 of the Geneva Conventions Act 1957, the applicant may be able to: obtain written consent from the Minister of Defence or a person authorised by the Minister. agree to an appropriate endorsement as a condition of registration, and would therefore not require consent from the Minister of Defence."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "manual"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Geneva Conventions Act provision itself is not supplied, so this answer relies on the Manual’s account and does not establish the complete statutory position or any exceptions.",
      "quotes": [],
      "authority": "none"
    }
  ],
  "declined": false,
